Every test server takes its port from its `HYDRA_*_PORT` variable, and a test fails on any port written anywhere else. The test frontends' scripts, the example frontends' mock-API origin, the Astro config and CI's start lines all named hydra's numbers directly: an Astro frontend on an overridden port listened on 3009 while the harness waited elsewhere, the examples fetched from whatever answered on 8888, and CI started Svelte and Vue on each other's ports, so each project tested the other frontend.
